{
  "file": "Guidance for national",
  "page": 100,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        231.10589599609375,
        21.884788513183594,
        277.722412109375,
        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "Guidance for",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        277.722412109375,
        21.884788513183594,
        349.1717834472656,
        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "national tuberculosis",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        351.4517822265625,
        21.884788513183594,
        407.7772216796875,
        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "programmes on",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        407.7772216796875,
        21.884788513183594,
        518.984130859375,
        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "the management of tuberculosis",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        518.984130859375,
        21.884788513183594,
        557.1551513671875,
        32.93328857421875
      ],
      "text": "in children",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightCn",
      "size": 9.5,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        83.188232421875,
        513.3800659179688,
        96.53973388671875
      ],
      "text": "It is often difficult to distinguish between congenital and neonatal TB but management",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        99.18475341796875,
        513.4950561523438,
        112.5362548828125
      ],
      "text": "is the same for both. Both forms will be referred to here as neonatal TB. The TB-exposed",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        115.1812744140625,
        321.421875,
        128.53277587890625
      ],
      "text": "neonate may be asymptomatic or symptomatic.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        139.68780517578125,
        513.3914184570312,
        153.039306640625
      ],
      "text": "Symptoms of neonatal TB are usually nonspecific and include lethargy, fever, poor",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        155.684326171875,
        513.46044921875,
        169.03582763671875
      ],
      "text": "feeding, low birth weight and poor weight gain. The clinical signs are also nonspecific",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        171.68084716796875,
        513.4375610351562,
        185.0323486328125
      ],
      "text": "and can include respiratory distress, non-resolving pneumonia, hepatosplenomegaly,",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        187.6773681640625,
        513.426025390625,
        201.02886962890625
      ],
      "text": "lymphadenopathy, abdominal distension with ascites, or a clinical picture of “neonatal",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        203.67388916015625,
        233.29737854003906,
        217.025390625
      ],
      "text": "sepsis” with disseminated TB.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        228.18035888671875,
        513.380126953125,
        241.5318603515625
      ],
      "text": "The diagnosis of TB should be included in the differential diagnosis of chronic neonatal",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        244.1768798828125,
        513.3799438476562,
        257.52838134765625
      ],
      "text": "infection with a poor response to antimicrobial therapy, congenital infections and",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        260.17340087890625,
        513.4146118164062,
        273.52490234375
      ],
      "text": "atypical pneumonia. The most important clue to the diagnosis of neonatal TB is a",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        276.169921875,
        513.3914184570312,
        289.52142333984375
      ],
      "text": "maternal history of TB or HIV infection. Critical points in the maternal history include",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        292.16644287109375,
        513.4259643554688,
        305.5179443359375
      ],
      "text": "non-resolving pneumonia, past treatment for TB, contact with an index case of TB and",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03939819335938,
        308.0939636230469,
        278.2163391113281,
        321.51446533203125
      ],
      "text": "(8) recent initiation of treatment for TB  .",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        334.3605041503906,
        467.1192626953125,
        351.0885009765625
      ],
      "text": "Management of the asymptomatic neonate exposed to maternal TB",
      "font": "Arial-BoldItalicMT",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        358.1000061035156,
        513.3683471679688,
        371.4515075683594
      ],
      "text": "TB disease should be excluded in a neonate born to a mother with suspected or",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        374.09649658203125,
        513.3914184570312,
        387.447998046875
      ],
      "text": "confirmed TB. Maternal infectiousness and drug susceptibility should be determined.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        390.0929870605469,
        513.4374389648438,
        403.4444885253906
      ],
      "text": "It is not necessary to separate the neonate from the mother if the mother does not",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        406.0204772949219,
        513.4144897460938,
        419.44097900390625
      ],
      "text": "It is not necessary to stop breast-feeding  have (or is not suspected of having) MDR-TB.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        422.0169677734375,
        513.3684692382812,
        435.4374694824219
      ],
      "text": "(3, 4).  While screening for TB disease or latent TB infection, BCG should not be given",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        438.08245849609375,
        513.4835205078125,
        451.4339599609375
      ],
      "text": "to neonates exposed to TB; the main reason for this is that BCG will interfere with the",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        454.0789489746094,
        513.391357421875,
        467.4304504394531
      ],
      "text": "interpretation of TST, reducing the effectiveness of the test for diagnosing infection.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        470.075439453125,
        513.4603881835938,
        483.42694091796875
      ],
      "text": "Further, as discussed in Chapter 5, BCG should not be given if the newborn or infant is",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        486.0719299316406,
        230.7327880859375,
        499.4234313964844
      ],
      "text": "confirmed to be HIV-positive.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        510.57843017578125,
        510.2864990234375,
        523.929931640625
      ],
      "text": "Asymptomatic neonates born to mothers with confirmed or suspected infectious drug-",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        526.5748901367188,
        513.3914184570312,
        539.9263916015625
      ],
      "text": "susceptible TB should receive isoniazid (10 mg/kg) for 6 months daily once TB disease",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        542.50244140625,
        513.4718627929688,
        555.9229125976562
      ],
      "text": "(9, 10) has been excluded  and should be regularly followed up to ensure that TB disease",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-LightItali",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        558.5679321289062,
        175.7972869873047,
        571.91943359375
      ],
      "text": "does not develop.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        583.0744018554688,
        513.4027709960938,
        596.4259033203125
      ],
      "text": "If an infant remains asymptomatic at the end of 6 months, treatment with isoniazid is",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        599.0709228515625,
        513.3683471679688,
        612.4224243164062
      ],
      "text": "stopped and a TST is performed. Usual practice is that BCG is given after 2 weeks if the",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        615.0674438476562,
        337.86676025390625,
        628.4189453125
      ],
      "text": "TST remains negative and the baby is HIV-negative.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        639.5739135742188,
        513.4949951171875,
        652.9254150390625
      ],
      "text": "If the mother is non-infectious, the infant should be screened for TB. If there is no",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        655.5704345703125,
        513.41455078125,
        668.9219360351562
      ],
      "text": "evidence of active TB, the infant should be regularly followed up to ensure that TB",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        671.5669555664062,
        360.2919006347656,
        684.91845703125
      ],
      "text": "disease does not develop, and IPT should be considered.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        696.0734252929688,
        513.3798828125,
        709.4249267578125
      ],
      "text": "If a diagnosis of TB is confirmed or the infant develops clinical signs suggestive of TB,",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        712.0699462890625,
        326.7807922363281,
        725.4214477539062
      ],
      "text": "treatment should be started under specialist care.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        736.576416015625,
        513.4489135742188,
        749.9279174804688
      ],
      "text": "Neonates born to mothers with MDR-TB or XDR-TB should be referred to a local expert",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        752.5729370117188,
        513.4373779296875,
        765.9244384765625
      ],
      "text": "in the management of this complicated problem. Infection control measures, such as",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        85.03929901123047,
        768.5693969726562,
        397.96588134765625,
        781.9208984375
      ],
      "text": "wearing a mask, are required to reduce the likelihood of MTCT.",
      "font": "FrutigerLTStd-Light",
      "size": 11.5,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        558.6439208984375,
        805.8439331054688,
        580.8839111328125,
        835.8439331054688
      ],
      "text": "81",
      "font": "HelveticaNeue-Light",
      "size": 20.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    }
  ]
}